## Java Implementation

```java
import java.util.*;

public class CommonElements {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int m = sc.nextInt();

        int[] a = new int[n];
        int[] b = new int[m];

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = sc.nextInt();
        for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) b[j] = sc.nextInt();

        Arrays.sort(a);
        Arrays.sort(b);

        int i = 0, j = 0;
        boolean found = false;
        while (i < n && j < m) {
            if (a[i] == b[j]) {
                System.out.println(a[i]);
                found = true;
                i++; j++;
            } else if (a[i] < b[j]) {
                i++;
            } else {
                j++;
            }
        }

        if (!found) System.out.println("No common elements");
    }
}
```

Compile & run:

```bash
javac CommonElements.java
java CommonElements
```

